				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				141,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Sky): Extract debug and workspace relays into dedicated installers\n\nSeparate the debug lifecycle, custom-editor, and workspace/decoration logic from the monolithic `Bridge.ts` into `Source/Function/Sky/Bridge/InstallDebug.ts` (implicitly created via import) and the new `InstallTasksAndDecorations.ts` module.\n\nThe `InstallTasksAndDecorations` file encapsulates relays for task execution, workspace edits, window focus, and the 16ms-batched decoration create/dispose flow, implementing a demultiplexing strategy for batched payloads. It also consolidates the six-action output-channel lifecycle and webview message/dispose relays.\n\nThis continues the modularization effort initiated in previous commits, ensuring each domain of Mountain-to-Sky IPC (debug, tasks, workspace, UI decorations) resides in a self-contained installer. The `Bridge.ts` entry point now delegates these complex relays via dynamic imports, preserving the existing DOM event dispatch shapes (`cel:*`) while reducing the static dependency graph and improving navigability.\n\nThe refactoring adheres to the PascalCase directory hierarchy and isolates specific domain logic to facilitate future maintenance and tree-shaking.",
			"SHA": "6487c94852597d6a202f4aa49c38d3e37b608386"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-05T05:00:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				140,
				17
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Sky): Modularize Bridge.ts into dedicated domain installers\n\nExtract the monolithic `Source/Function/Sky/Bridge.ts` into a hierarchy of self-contained modules under `Source/Function/Sky/Bridge/`. This migration separates concerns by domain: commands, statusbar, editor/output, progress/terminal, and diagnostic probes now live in distinct files (`InstallCommands.ts`, `InstallStatusbar.ts`, `InstallEditorAndOutput.ts`, etc.) or grouped relays (`InstallSimpleRelays.ts`, `InstallFanOut.ts`).\n\nThe refactor utilizes dynamic imports to load these modules asynchronously, hydrating local symbols (e.g., `BuildOpenArg`, `ShowProgress`) with the factory results. This reduces the static dependency graph, improves tree-shaking, and isolates complex logic like `CelDispatchTracking` and `ApplyHtmlToWebview` into dedicated utilities.\n\nCrucially, this structure preserves the exact runtime behavior of the `Register` loop while making the codebase navigable. The `InstallDeadChannelListeners` module specifically activates the nine previously dormant Mountain-to-Sky event channels (tree-view, configuration, security incidents), ensuring that backend state changes are faithfully propagated to the workbench without silent failures.",
			"SHA": "e4d1bf432fc1721a57c18dabb5c7e9184128e464"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1781446819128
}